const data = {
  eyebrow: 'Prevent, Redistribute, Repurpose & Recover',
  title: 'Keep Food and Resources at Their Highest Value',
  lead: 'Terra Nexus helps food businesses prevent loss, redesign operations, create markets for surplus and byproducts, select recovery pathways, and build circular programs that improve economics and environmental performance.',
  primaryCta: { label: 'Discuss Your Food-Waste Opportunity', href: '/contact/' },
  secondaryCta: { label: 'Explore Our Capabilities', href: '/capabilities/' },
  metaTitle: 'Food Waste: Prevention, Diversion & Recovery | Terra Nexus',
  metaDescription: 'Terra Nexus helps food businesses prevent loss, redesign operations, create markets for surplus and byproducts, select recovery pathways, and build circular programs that improve economics and environmental performance.',
  orientation: [
    'Food loss and waste can occur before harvest, during storage and transportation, in processing, in manufacturing, at retail, in foodservice, or after purchase. The causes and solutions are different at every stage. A forecasting problem should not be treated like a processing byproduct. An edible surplus should not be managed like contaminated material. A valuable ingredient stream should not be sent to a lower-value recovery pathway because the market, logistics, or quality requirements were never developed.',
    'The most effective approach is to understand where food, nutrients, materials, energy, labor, and money are being lost and then prioritize the highest practical use. Once food or a byproduct leaves its intended use, part of its value has often already been lost — the business has paid for raw materials, production, labor, energy, water, packaging, storage, transportation, and management. A lower-value recovery pathway may reduce disposal cost or create revenue, but it rarely recovers the full value embedded in the original product. Terra Nexus helps clients treat food waste as an integrated portfolio of prevention, redistribution, product, operational, market, and recovery opportunities, and compare prevention with downstream pathways using the complete economics rather than only the disposal fee or revenue per tonne.',
  ],
  performanceCategories: [
    { title: 'Lower Cost and Better Yield', items: ['Reduced raw-material loss, giveaway, overproduction, spoilage, and rework', 'Improved process yield, inventory turns, and shelf life', 'Lower hauling, treatment, disposal, and compliance cost', 'Improved labor, energy, water, packaging, and asset utilization', 'Fewer quality failures and write-offs'] },
    { title: 'More Food Kept in Use', items: ['Better matching of supply and demand', 'Earlier identification of surplus', 'Stronger donation, rescue, markdown, and secondary-market pathways', 'Improved logistics and cold-chain coordination', 'Reduced loss across farms, processors, distribution, retail, and foodservice'] },
    { title: 'New Revenue and Product Value', items: ['Sale of co-products and byproducts', 'New ingredients, feedstocks, food products, feed, materials, or services', 'Improved valuation of side streams', 'New customer and channel relationships', 'Licensing, partnership, or venture opportunities'] },
    { title: 'Improved Environmental Performance', items: ['Reduced embedded land, water, energy, and emissions associated with wasted food', 'Lower disposal and treatment impacts', 'Recovery of nutrients, energy, and materials', 'Improved circularity and resource efficiency', 'Stronger corporate target and reporting performance where supported by evidence'] },
    { title: 'Greater Resilience and Collaboration', items: ['More flexible outlets for surplus and byproducts', 'Stronger coordination among suppliers, operations, customers, recovery partners, community organizations, and regulators', 'Reduced exposure to disposal capacity, commodity volatility, and changing rules', 'Better visibility into material flows and root causes'] },
  ],
  systemSteps: [
    { title: 'Define the Objective and Scope', body: 'The starting point may be cost reduction, waste targets, operational excellence, new revenue, a byproduct challenge, regulatory change, food donation, circularity, facility investment, or a new technology.', detail: 'Terra Nexus helps define the facilities, products, materials, geographies, participants, data, commercial objective, and decision boundary.' },
    { title: 'Measure Material and Value Flows', body: 'A useful assessment shows where material comes from, why it is lost, what quality it retains, where it goes, what it costs, and who controls the decision. Relevant information may include material type, quantity, composition, and variability; edible versus inedible portions; quality, safety, contamination, and shelf life; process, product, line, shift, location, supplier, and customer; seasonality and timing; handling, storage, and transportation; current outlet, treatment, cost, revenue, and contractual terms; embedded raw-material and processing value; and root causes, ownership, and decision rights.', detail: 'Terra Nexus helps create a material-and-value baseline that supports operational, commercial, investment, and reporting decisions.' },
    { title: 'Prioritize Prevention and Highest-Value Pathways', body: 'Opportunities should be compared using more than environmental preference. Relevant factors include avoidable cost and recoverable value; food safety, quality, and legal requirements; customer and market demand; material consistency and scale; logistics and infrastructure; capital and operating requirements; partner capability and counterparty risk; emissions and environmental performance; implementation timing and scalability; and organizational ownership and change required.', detail: 'Terra Nexus helps clients build a prioritized portfolio rather than forcing every material into one technology or outlet.' },
    { title: 'Develop the Business Case and Market', body: 'A potential byproduct or surplus market must work for both the generator and the buyer.', detail: 'Terra Nexus helps evaluate product or feedstock specifications; processing, stabilization, testing, packaging, and storage; volume, seasonality, and reliability; customer applications and alternatives; pricing, avoided cost, revenue, margin, and logistics; capital, working capital, and payback; contractual responsibilities, liability, and quality; ownership of claims, credits, or environmental attributes; and partner, customer, and route-to-market strategy.' },
    { title: 'Select Technology and Partners Around the Operating Need', body: 'Technology may support forecasting, measurement, resale, donation, separation, processing, upcycling, composting, digestion, treatment, or resource recovery. Technology is selected after the material, operating, and commercial problem is clear — not as the starting point.', detail: 'Terra Nexus helps clients evaluate technology readiness, feedstock fit, integration, performance claims, utilities, maintenance, permitting, output markets, vendor quality, financing, and scale.' },
    { title: 'Build and Launch the Operating Model', body: 'Implementation may require new procedures, segregation, quality controls, inventory rules, training, equipment, data capture, contracts, logistics, customer development, partner coordination, and reporting.', detail: 'Terra Nexus helps design roles, workflows, controls, decision rights, pilots, implementation plans, and scale gates. We can also manage recurring workstreams within client-owned programs.' },
    { title: 'Measure Financial, Operational, and Environmental Performance', body: 'Programs should track the outcomes relevant to the decision, which may include tonnes prevented, redistributed, repurposed, recycled, or recovered; product and process yield; cost avoided and revenue created; edible food kept in use; material quality and outlet reliability; emissions, energy, water, nutrients, or landfill diversion; customer, community, and partner outcomes; and capital performance and operating reliability.', detail: 'Terra Nexus helps align measurement, accounting, claims, and management review so reported results match the actual operating system.' },
  ],
  audiencePathways: [
